libzello (0.1.6-1) unstable; urgency=low

  * tx: cap the WS poll timeout to time-until-next-drain while a TX
    is active. Callers that ran poll() with a 100 ms timeout were
    blocking the full 100 ms between drains, capping outbound rate
    at one frame per 100 ms (9.6 kHz) while the producer pushed at
    16 kHz. Ring grew unbounded, audio arrived late at the Zello
    server, and listeners heard Opus PLC fill the gaps with static.
  * tx: outbound packet_id now starts at 1 and increments per frame
    instead of being zero on every packet. The published API doc
    says packet_id is ignored on outbound, but the official JS SDK
    (zello-channel-api outgoingMessage.js) actually sends a sequence
    and the server-side path appears to use it for re-timing.
  * tx: reset the Opus encoder state at the start of each new stream
    (OPUS_RESET_STATE). Listeners start a fresh decoder per
    stream_id, so residual prediction state from the previous stream
    used to come out as garbled audio in the first few frames.
  * tx: serialize ring reset against the producer thread via a new
    tx_streaming atomic gate. start_tx opens it AFTER zeroing the
    ring indices; stop_tx closes it BEFORE flagging the drain;
    send_pcm drops samples while the gate is closed. Eliminates a
    race where the producer could push samples into a stale write
    index and have them overwritten by the reset.
  * tx: drain at a strict frame_ms cadence — tx_next_encode_ms is
    reset to (now + frame_ms) after each drain instead of advancing
    by frame_ms from the previous schedule. Stops the back-to-back
    burst drains that arrived at Zello listeners as garbled audio.
  * rx: add a DEBUG log per inbound audio packet (stream_id, opus
    bytes, decoded sample count, sample rate). Lets you compare wire
    sizes between our outbound and what live clients push.
  * reconnect: drop the cached refresh_token on logon failure. When
    another client logs in with the same account the server evicts
    our session and invalidates the refresh_token. Without this fix
    we kept retrying with the dead token forever and got "no
    permission" on every reconnect; now we fall back to a fresh
    username+password logon on the next attempt and recover as soon
    as the conflicting client exits.
  * tests: new test_codec_roundtrip program that loads a 16-bit
    mono WAV, encodes through libzello's Opus + Zello packet
    wrapping, unwraps + decodes, and writes the reconstruction. Used
    to verify the codec/protocol path independently of WS/server
    behaviour when diagnosing audio garbling.

 -- Brian <brian@kerchunk.net>  Fri, 22 May 2026 00:00:00 +0000

libzello (0.1.1-1) unstable; urgency=low

  * Replace libwebsockets with a native WebSocket implementation
    (OpenSSL TLS + non-blocking POSIX sockets + RFC 6455 framing).
    Removes the multi-second lws_service stalls that were starving
    the TX path.
  * Make the client thread-safe with a recursive control-plane mutex
    plus a lock-free SPSC ring for the PCM data plane; a dedicated
    service thread paces Opus encode+send at the configured frame
    cadence (default 60 ms) so producers can push frames without
    blocking.
  * Build-Depends switched from libwebsockets-dev to libssl-dev.
  * pkg-config Requires.private now lists openssl opus libcjson.

 -- Brian <brian@kerchunk.net>  Thu, 21 May 2026 00:00:00 +0000

libzello (0.1.0-1) unstable; urgency=low

  * Initial release.
  * WS transport via libwebsockets, control plane via libcjson,
    audio via libopus (16 kHz mono, 60 ms frames).
  * Friends & Family (wss://zello.io/ws) and Zello Work
    (wss://zellowork.io/ws/<network>) supported via server_url.
  * Refresh-token reconnect with exponential backoff.

 -- Brian <brian@kerchunk.net>  Wed, 20 May 2026 16:00:00 +0000
